# Documentation conventions
- QuizContext charter/core scope outrank CareerContext reference exports.
- Tickets describe one shippable unit, with status, dependencies, scope, out of scope, and testable acceptance criteria.
- Update `devTickets_next.md` and `devCompletion.md` as part of implementing a ticket, not as a separate documentation sprint.
- Keep requirements concise and implementation-neutral unless an explicit decision is already established.
- Include only representative file paths in reference notes; do not paste entire source trees into docs.
- Mark proposed vs implemented behaviour clearly; OpenAPI describes implemented behaviour only.
- Do not read or reproduce `docs/reference/source-extract/` unless the current task specifically benefits from it.
